 want this what you want is  this  straight back straight shoulders not to  the front but  back and a straight neck not forward but  here  now i get it it does look weird if you  walk like this everywhere  [Music]  [Music]  but you do need to improve your posture  as much  as possible so that you can still look  natural  and not weird now the first thing that  you need to do is to get rid of your bad  habits this is the most important thing  that you have to start with  every time you catch yourself slouching  while you sit and work on the computer  sit up straight when you catch yourself  looking at your phone with your head  forward and down  bring your phone up and make your neck  straight now  the second thing that you can do to  improve your bad body posture  is stretching exercises now  there are actually many that you can do  and they all work great but i'm just  gonna give you the seven  best according to me of course so let's  start with the first one  now this one is easy all you need is a  door frame all you need to do is stand  in front of the door frame  take one step forward with your body  weight on it and bring your arms  up above your head hold it there for  about  15 to 30 seconds you'll feel your pec  stretch and your back straightening as  well  now you can hold your arms here at  different positions so lower your arms a  little  right next to you and keep it there for  15 seconds and lastly lower it even more  and keep it there for 15  seconds so this helps you to get out of  this slouchy forward position  to open up your back is straight your  shoulders is back and straight  your neck is up and straight as well  this is what you want  the second stretch you can easily do at  home works for your lower back  and this is the superman lay down on the  floor then raise your legs off the  ground  and stretch your arms out right in front  of you do three sets of 12 reps  the next exercise is going to help these  back muscles that's been  weakened because of this forward slouchy  movement all the time  and this muscle group is called the  thoracic area so how are you going to  stretch it and make it stronger  face pulls you can do face pulls at the  gym or at home with a resistance band  if you don't go to the gym if you work  out at home and you want a resistance  band i'll add some good options for you  in the video description down below  as always but you can also work out  these muscles  without any equipment at home with the  door frame  all you got to do is stand in front of  the door frame arms on the frame  lean back and pull yourself forward  another great exercise is that you can  stretch your back with a foam  roller if you don't have one then i'll  add one for in the video description  that you can check out  but then again if you don't want to buy  one you can just use  towels just take three to four towels  together and roll them up  then just put them on the ground lay  down on it with your spine  all the way from your tailbone to your  head and if the towels are too short  just get a pillow for your head now you  can use another towel or a broom or even  a golf club  and move it with both hands from your  legs over your head  and back again and then you just do this  slowly for one to two minutes depending  on how your body feels  now if for some reason you don't have  another towel or a broomstick or  whatever to use  with both hands then you can also do  angel stretches  so start by moving your arms from the  bottom next to your sides  all the way up over your head and back  and again do this for one to two minutes  another exercise that you can do if for  some reason you don't like lying on the  floor  is the wall posture exercise if you  can't do this  really well then you know that your  posture is probably not good  or your body is too stiff you can  actually do this with me right now  go to the wall put your hips back  shoulders  and head against the wall now your whole  body posture  will be in the right position your feet  can actually be a few inches  away from the wall remember not to tilt  your head  or chin down head straight and chin up  now we're gonna do snow angels or some  people call them butterflies  but not the full movement alright bring  your arms up next to you  against the wall with your elbows and  the back of your hands  against the wall now move your arms over  your head  and back again now if you've got a  stability ball at home then  use it because it's great for your body  posture  if you want one at home then i'll add  one for in the video description that  you can check out now all you gotta do  is get on it drop your hips off the ball  as much as you can  bring your arms up straight over your  head and just lay over the ball  and stay there for 10 to 30 seconds  depending  on how your body feels now if you don't  have a stability ball  if you don't want one then just hang i  really mean just  a hand you can do it at the gym before  you do your pull-ups  just hang on the pull-up bar  [Music]  with your feet back and stretch your  front side  you can do this for 30 to 50 seconds  depending on how your body feels  now apart from those bad habits that you  have to leave and  the stretching exercises that you can do  to improve your body posture  you can also get these mesh back support  cushion things for your chair  my wife and i use them all the time and  it makes a  big difference you don't have to sit  with bad posture  and back pain the whole day while  working and as always i'll add it for  you in the video description so you can  check it out  now if you really struggle with bad body  posture then you can get  a back posture support brace like this  one  many people use it and love it you can  check out all the great customer reviews  about it on  amazon now always remember this good  styling  good grooming and great body posture  always needs to go hand in hand  cheers guys


